            "abstract": "With the full Sloan Digital Sky Survey the statistical errors will be below 1 percent for the <b>galaxy</b>-<b>galaxy</b> correlations and significantly larger for QSO-<b>galaxy</b> correlations. Thus accurate constraints on parameters of the <b>galaxy</b> halo occupation distribution can be obtained from small scale measurements and on the bias parameter from large scales. "
